There are several ways to center a div in CSS, depending on the structure of the HTML and the desired level of complexity. Here are a few common methods:

1. Using the `margin` property:
```
div {
  margin: 0 auto;
}
```
This method works by setting the left and right margins to `0`, and the top and bottom margins to `auto`. This will center the div horizontally within its parent element
